warning[F0805]: this says that `x` matches one of these patterns
  --> test/cli/commands/mutate_list.fren:56:28
   |
56 |     ensure chained: ok? or x = 4 or x = 6
   |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ equations of one expression with values that patterns write
   |
   = help: `fren fix` can fix this
   = note: `manual_pattern_test` is `warn` by default
   = help: to allow it, `set_option fren.lint.manual_pattern_test "allow"`
help: write `x is 4 | 6`
   |
56 -     ensure chained: ok? or x = 4 or x = 6
56 +     ensure chained: ok? or x is 4 | 6
   |

warning[F0712]: this `Bool` expression can be simpler
  --> test/cli/commands/mutate_list.fren:66:60
   |
66 |     ensure exclusive: at_most_one?(x = 1, x = 2, x = 3) or exactly_one?(x > 3)
   |                                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `exactly_one?` of one argument is that argument
   |
   = help: `fren fix` can fix this
   = note: `nonminimal_bool` is `warn` by default
   = help: to allow it, `set_option fren.lint.nonminimal_bool "allow"`
help: write `x > 3`
   |
66 -     ensure exclusive: at_most_one?(x = 1, x = 2, x = 3) or exactly_one?(x > 3)
66 +     ensure exclusive: at_most_one?(x = 1, x = 2, x = 3) or x > 3
   |

warning[F0810]: `x` is never negative, so it can be a `Nat`
  --> test/cli/commands/mutate_list.fren:52:21
   |
52 |     assume bounded: x >= 0 and x <= LIMIT
   |                     ^^^^^^ `x` is at least 0 by this assumption
   |
   = note: a `Nat` input brings this assumption with its type
   = note: an instance must then bind `x` to a `Nat`
   = help: declare `x: Nat`, and remove `x >= 0` from `bounded`, where nothing binds `x` to an `Int`
   = note: `manual_nat` is `warn` by default
   = help: to allow it, `set_option fren.lint.manual_nat "allow"`

